# Banking Microservices Application

This repository contains a Spring Boot-based banking microservice system built to simulate a real-world digital banking flow with account management, transaction processing, fraud detection, payment integration, and notifications.

The architecture follows an event-driven microservices pattern using:
- Spring Boot 3 / Java
- PostgreSQL for service data stores
- Redis for OTP and transient data
- Apache Kafka for async communication between services
- Feign clients for synchronous service-to-service calls
- Razorpay for payment order creation and webhook processing
- Docker Compose for service orchestration

## 1. Project Structure

At the root of the project:
- account-service
- transaction-service
- payment-service
- fraud-detection-service
- notification-service
- api-gateway
- docker-compose.yml
- .env

## 2. Services Overview

### 2.1 account-service
Port: 8081

Responsibilities:
- Create bank accounts
- Fetch account details and balances
- Credit and deduct balances
- Block/unblock accounts
- Maintain account status and daily transaction limits

Data Store:
- PostgreSQL database (`account_db`)

Key APIs:
- GET /api/v1/accounts
- POST /api/v1/accounts
- GET /api/v1/accounts/{accountNumber}
- GET /api/v1/accounts/{accountNumber}/balance
- PUT /api/v1/accounts/{accountNumber}/block
- PUT /api/v1/accounts/{accountNumber}/unblock
- PUT /api/v1/accounts/{accountNumber}/deduct
- PUT /api/v1/accounts/{accountNumber}/credit

### 2.2 transaction-service
Port: 8082

Responsibilities:
- Transfer money between accounts
- Handle transfer-with-payment flow
- Validate OTP for suspicious transactions
- Store transaction history and statuses
- Publish and consume Kafka events
- Coordinate payment and fraud workflows

Data Store:
- PostgreSQL database (`transaction_db`)
- Redis (OTP storage and verification)

Key APIs:
- POST /api/v1/transactions/transfer
- POST /api/v1/transactions/transfer-with-payment
- GET /api/v1/transactions/{transactionId}
- GET /api/v1/transactions/history/{accountNumber}
- POST /api/v1/transactions/{transactionId}/verify

### 2.3 payment-service
Port: 8084

Responsibilities:
- Create Razorpay orders for transactions
- Keep payment records in the database
- Receive Razorpay webhook events
- Emit payment.completed and payment.failed events to Kafka

Data Store:
- PostgreSQL database (`payment_db`)

Key APIs:
- POST /api/v1/payments/create-order
- POST /api/v1/payments/webhook

### 2.4 fraud-detection-service
Port: 8083

Responsibilities:
- Listen to transaction initiation events
- Check sender balance and determine if a transaction seems suspicious
- Trigger verification-required flow for risky transactions
- Publish fraud.clean or verification events based on result

Kafka interaction:
- Consumes: transaction.initiated
- Produces: verification.required, fraud.check.clean

### 2.5 notification-service
Port: 8085

Responsibilities:
- Consume event notifications from Kafka
- Send alerts/log notifications for OTP generation, transaction status, refunds, fraud alerts, and payment results

Kafka interaction:
- Consumes:
  - transaction.otp.generated
  - transaction.completed
  - fraud.detected
  - transaction.refunded
  - payment.completed
  - payment.failed

This service is mainly a notification/logging layer in the current implementation and logs alerts to the application console instead of sending real emails/SMS.

### 2.6 api-gateway
Port: 9090

Responsibilities:
- Central entry point for client-facing requests
- Exposes routing to downstream microservices
- Connects to account-service, transaction-service, and payment-service

## 3. Technology Stack

- Java 17 / Spring Boot 3.x
